---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const providerOutput = `{
  "metrics": [
    {
      "subject": "src/app/main.go",
      "provider": "foo",
      "values": { "foo.some_metric": 42 }
    }
  ]
}`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Providers"
  description="Understand filesystem, scc, and custom metric providers."
  current="/providers/"
>
  <article class="doc">
    <h1>Providers</h1>
    <p>
      Considered itself defines almost no metrics. Providers collect metrics,
      and the policy engine evaluates their output.
    </p>

    <h2>Built in</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>filesystem.bytes</code> measures file size.</li>
      <li><code>filesystem.longest_line</code> measures the longest line in Unicode characters.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Bundled external provider</h2>
    <p>
      <code>considered-scc</code> wraps the vendored <code>scc</code> submodule
      and provides metrics such as <code>scc.code_lines</code>,
      <code>scc.comment_lines</code>, and <code>scc.complexity</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Custom providers</h2>
    <p>
      For a metric namespaced <code>foo.*</code>, Considered runs an executable
      named <code>considered-foo</code>.
    </p>

    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={"considered-foo --root <dir> --json --exclude-dir .git --exclude-dir node_modules"} />

    <p>
      Providers must accept <code>--root</code>, <code>--json</code>, and repeated
      <code>--exclude-dir</code> arguments. Considered passes directory exclusions
      derived from the configuration, including <code>.git</code>, so providers
      can skip those directories before collecting metrics. The exact list
      depends on the repository's exclusions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Print only the JSON result to stdout. Send diagnostics to stderr and exit
      non-zero on failure. Considered runs the providers referenced by configured
      standards; an unavailable or failed provider makes the check fail.
    </p>
    <p>The provider prints JSON to stdout:</p>

    <CodeBlock lang="json" code={providerOutput} />

    <p>
      <code>subject</code> is repository-relative. <code>provider</code> is
      optional and defaults to the metric namespace.
    </p>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
